<template>
  <section>
    <h2 class="pdx-txt-heading section-heading">Why an app needs one</h2>
    <p class="pdx-txt-small pdx-ink-muted">
      A <code>&lt;pdx-dialog&gt;</code> lives in your template, next to the state that opens it. A question asked from
      a function — "discard changes?" in a save handler, a confirmation before a delete — has no template to live in.
      The service puts it in the queue, and the outlet is the one place in the page that renders it. Mount it
      <strong>once</strong>, in the app shell, as the last child of the layout:
    </p>
    <pre class="pdx-txt-mono shell"><code>&lt;!-- app.pdx --&gt;
&lt;pdx-app-layout&gt;
  …
  &lt;pdx-router-outlet&gt;&lt;/pdx-router-outlet&gt;
&lt;/pdx-app-layout&gt;
&lt;pdx-overlay-outlet&gt;&lt;/pdx-overlay-outlet&gt;</code></pre>
    <p class="pdx-txt-small pdx-ink-muted">
      A form's <code>warnUnsaved</code> guard asks through the same queue, and mounts an outlet itself when the page has none.
    </p>
  </section>
</template>

<style scoped>
  .shell { margin: var(--pdx-space-md) 0; }
</style>
